35,2,1,talk,Servas,,It is a reminder that people are the heartbeat of science. We must ensure the chosen project has the hands to do the work.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've noticed some worrying trends. The cost of basic logistics is rising, but some central subsidies are still holding. It's a bit uneven.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Oh no! I found out that some of the big machines were broken for weeks because there wasn't a repair person! That's a problem!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, it seems we are in agreement. My findings suggest that administrative lapses and biological volatility are the primary thieves of time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests that ""high-impact"" promises often fail to materialize. Stability and a track record of delivery are more valuable than ambition.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, stability is a virtue, but we must not stifle the spirit of discovery. We just need the right support.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, exactly. But if the grant doesn't cover the rising costs of field work, even the best spirit will be crushed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried that if we pick a project that needs those broken machines, they'll just be stuck! We should pick someone who doesn't need them.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A charmingly simplistic solution, Kenji. However, we should perhaps favor a candidate whose methodology is resilient to such systemic failures.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Resilience is proven by past results, not by the promises in a proposal. I am looking for a candidate who delivers on time.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,Let us remember that a seed needs both good soil and a gardener. The gardener is the most precious part.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. I hope the candidates we see have a realistic plan for their technical staff, given the current market.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,I just want everyone to be happy and the science to actually happen! Let's hope the candidates are ready for this!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I suspect we will find that some candidates are far more optimistic about their timelines than reality allows.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Optimism is a liability in a multi-year grant. I will be voting for the one with the most grounded approach.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
